SDK DPAA ethtool: demote "phy device not initialized" to netdev_dbg

The SDK DPAA ethtool ops are PHY-only -- every callback NULL-checks
priv->mac_dev->phy_dev and returns -ENODEV when no PHY is bound.
On fixed-link / SFP+ cages (Mono Gateway DK and similar boards that
intentionally bypass phylink), phy_dev is legitimately NULL for the
lifetime of the netdev.  Userspace ethtool ioctls then flood dmesg
with "phy device not initialized" -- eight call sites in this file
all print the exact same string.

Two of the eight call sites already use netdev_dbg
(dpa_get_link_ksettings, dpa_set_wol), confirming the original
author considered this a benign condition.  The remaining six
print at netdev_err (KERN_ERR), which on a board with five SFP+
MACs produces dozens of identical lines per VyOS interface commit.

Demote the six remaining sites to netdev_dbg to match the existing
pattern.  Semantics are unchanged -- every callsite still returns
-ENODEV (or void) so userspace correctly sees the operation as
unsupported; only the kernel log noise is suppressed.

Sites changed (in dpaa_ethtool.c, after SDK source drop):
  dpa_set_ksettings, dpa_nway_reset, dpa_get_pauseparam,
  dpa_set_pauseparam, dpa_get_eee, dpa_set_eee.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_dpaa/dpaa_ethtool.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_dpaa/dpaa_ethtool.c
@@ -125,7 +125,7 @@
 		return -ENODEV;
 	}
 	if (unlikely(priv->mac_dev->phy_dev == NULL)) {
-		netdev_err(net_dev, "phy device not initialized\n");
+		netdev_dbg(net_dev, "phy device not initialized\n");
 		return -ENODEV;
 	}
 
@@ -180,7 +180,7 @@
 		return -ENODEV;
 	}
 	if (unlikely(priv->mac_dev->phy_dev == NULL)) {
-		netdev_err(net_dev, "phy device not initialized\n");
+		netdev_dbg(net_dev, "phy device not initialized\n");
 		return -ENODEV;
 	}
 
@@ -212,7 +212,7 @@
 
 	phy_dev = mac_dev->phy_dev;
 	if (unlikely(phy_dev == NULL)) {
-		netdev_err(net_dev, "phy device not initialized\n");
+		netdev_dbg(net_dev, "phy device not initialized\n");
 		return;
 	}
 
@@ -240,7 +240,7 @@
 
 	phy_dev = mac_dev->phy_dev;
 	if (unlikely(phy_dev == NULL)) {
-		netdev_err(net_dev, "phy device not initialized\n");
+		netdev_dbg(net_dev, "phy device not initialized\n");
 		return -ENODEV;
 	}
 
@@ -327,7 +327,7 @@
 	}
 
 	if (unlikely(priv->mac_dev->phy_dev == NULL)) {
-		netdev_err(net_dev, "phy device not initialized\n");
+		netdev_dbg(net_dev, "phy device not initialized\n");
 		return -ENODEV;
 	}
 
@@ -345,7 +345,7 @@
 	}
 
 	if (unlikely(priv->mac_dev->phy_dev == NULL)) {
-		netdev_err(net_dev, "phy device not initialized\n");
+		netdev_dbg(net_dev, "phy device not initialized\n");
